\cf0  \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl374\sb216

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Task\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl260\sb144

\f0\b0\fs20 \cf0 Create an archetype to define a C struct definition for the classes in any model. The struct should contain member data for each attribute, but you may assume that all attributes are of type 'int'. Output your results to ex3.c. \
Each class is related to its attributes via R102 in the xtUML metamodel. First, select the classes in the model by using the method from the first two exercises. Using the 
\i .Name
\i0  property of the objects, form the C 'struct <name>' declaration for each class object.\
Then, for each object in the set generated by the previous operation, select the attributes related to the class objects by R102. There will possibly be zero to many attributes, so a 
\i .select many
\i0  operation is needed.\
Iterating across this attribute set using a 
\i .for each
\i0  loop, the C 'int <name>' declaration can be implemented with the 
\i attr_inst.Name
\i0 . \
\pard\pardeftab720\ri0\sl374\sb216

